"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIt was a somewhat difficult book for me. Not because the content is hard, but because the protagonist's painful emotions are well-revealed in the author's expressions and word choices.  \nI felt a similar hardship as when I read 's 28 in the past.  \n\nThe emotions felt by the husband, brother-in-law, and sister towards  are all different. There is no perspective of the protagonist  herself.  \n\nThis work also seems to be a book that needs to be read several times.  \n\nThe immersion and liveliness given by 's expressions and word choices make me a bit afraid to read her other works.  \nEspecially Human Acts seems like something I'll have to read with great determination."